==Quarter-finals==

===Austria vs Hungary===
{{see also|Austria–Hungary football rivalry}}
An extremely tough game prevented the two teams from truly showing the technical skills they possessed. Austria took an early lead with [[Johann Horvath]], who finished a well-organised team move. Austria doubled their lead in the early stages of the second half. Shortly after, Hungary got one back thanks to a penalty caused by [[Karl Sesta]]. The match hung in the balance until Hungary lost two players: [[Imre Markos]] was red carded and [[István Avar]] got injured. After that, Austria comfortably cruised to the victory.<ref name="fiedler" />

